<title>UK: UK Oct net consumer credit up s/a 856 mln stg.</title>
<headline>UK Oct net consumer credit up s/a 856 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England released the following seasonally-adjusted consumer credit data</p>
<p>-NET LENDING (previously released data in brackets, in MLN stg)</p>
<p>					    Oct	 Sept	    Oct 95</p>
<p> Total net lending		    2,631     2,441 (2,420)  1,765</p>
<p> -- Consumer credit		     856     1,041 (1,067)    850</p>
<p> -- On dwellings			1,775     1,399 (1,353)    915</p>
<p>BREAKDOWN OF NET CONSUMER LENDING BY SOURCE</p>
<p> -- Banks				 622	 859  (890)	 732</p>
<p> -- Building Soc			35	  32   (32)	   27</p>
<p> -- Other specialist lenders	199	 141  (137)	 116</p>
<p> -- Retailers			    2	  13   (12)	  -19</p>
<p> -- Insurance co			-2	  -4   (-4)	   -6</p>
<p> -- Credit card			 257	 146  (149)	 225</p>
<p>CONSUMER CREDIT (seasonally adjusted in pct)</p>
<p> Consumer credit mth/mth	    1.2	 1.5  (1.5)	 1.4</p>
<p>		     3mth annualised  18.0	19.7 (20.2)     13.7</p>
<p>		     6mth annualised  16.8	17.8 (18.1)     13.6</p>
<p>		     year-on-year     16.0	16.1 (16.2)     13.2</p>
<p> Total Personal borrowing mth/mth 0.6	 0.5  (0.5)	 0.4</p>
<p>		     3mth annualised  6.7	 6.6  (6.7)	 5.0</p>
<p>		     6mth annualised  6.5	 6.4  (6.4)	 5.0</p>
<p>		     year-on-year     6.1	 5.9  (5.9)	 5.4</p>
<p> Secured on Dwellings mth/mth     0.4	 0.3  (0.3)	 0.2</p>
<p>		     3mth annualised  4.9	 4.5  (4.5)	 3.7</p>
<p>		     6mth annualised  4.8	 4.5  (4.5)	 3.7</p>
<p>		     year-on-year     4.5	 4.2  (4.3)	 4.3</p>
<p>Note - Consensus forecast was for a 1.07 billion stg rise in</p>
<p>net credit.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
